---
/**
 * p61 · Plozz — Cowl
 *
 * A receiver and a display in one body: the shell draws in over the glass and
 * spreads out under it, so the picture sits back in a cowl. The top of it lies
 * in that shade and the light reaches it low, from the left. Nothing draws the
 * signal — the cowl and what it keeps off the glass do.
 *
 * Eleven blue tones. The shell is banded off its own distance field; the
 * shoulders the cowl steps out onto face upward and catch the key light, while
 * the picture darkens under the neck. The face sits on the plain screen tone
 * with a pixel of air all round.
 */
